# Public keys allowed to sign release tags (`v*`).
#
# Format: one entry per line, matching ssh-keygen's allowed_signers
# format: <principal>[,principal] <key-type> <key-data> [<comment>]
#
# Principal: an email or identifier — purely a label, used in
# verification error messages. Use the maintainer's webflow address
# so audit logs name the human.
#
# On `git push` of a v* tag, the release.yml workflow verifies:
#   1. The tag object is annotated (not lightweight).
#   2. `git tag -v <tag>` resolves the signer's pubkey against this
#      file and reports a good signature.
#
# Add a new maintainer key: open a PR. CODEOWNERS routes it to
# @webflow/infrastructure-security for review. Tag-signing is the
# chokepoint of the signed-release pipeline; treat additions as
# the high-trust event that they are.

